Now make the icon preparation BLOCKING before launch (so icons are ready when game boots) instead of a fire-and-forget spawn. Replace the spawn block:

```rust
// Oyun içi ikonlar: manifest arka planda yazılır (ağ) — açılışı engellemez
{
    let inst_icons = inst.clone();
    tauri::async_runtime::spawn(async move {
        write_mod_icons(&inst_icons).await;
    });
}
```
→ make it await directly before launch_game (icons ready at game boot). It runs after ensure_installed, before the "starting" emit. Downloads ~60 small PNGs sequentially... hmm my implementation downloads SEQUENTIALLY in a loop — 60 files × latency ≈ 10-30s! TOO SLOW for blocking. Need parallel downloads. Let me use futures_util::stream::iter + buffer_unordered(16). futures-util is a dependency ✓ (Cargo.toml has futures-util 0.3).

```rust
use futures_util::StreamExt;
let tasks: Vec<(String, String)> = icons.iter().filter(...).map(|(n,u)| (n.clone(), u.clone())).collect();
let results = futures_util::stream::iter(...)
```
Simpler: spawn tokio tasks per url and await all:
```rust
let mut jobs = Vec::new();
for (name, url) in &icons {
    if url.starts_with("data:") { manifest.push...; continue; }
    manifest.push_str(name); manifest.push('\t'); manifest.push_str(url); manifest.push('\n');
    let url2 = url.clone();
    let dir2 = icons_dir.clone();
    jobs.push(tokio::spawn(async move {
        let file = dir2.join(icon_cache_name(&url2));
        if file.exists() { return; }
        if let Ok(resp) = crate::core::http_client().get(&url2).send().await {
            if resp.status().is_success() {
                if let Ok(bytes) = resp.bytes().await {
                    let _ = std::fs::write(&file, &bytes);
                }
            }
        }
    }));
}
for j in jobs { let _ = j.await; }
```
Parallel ✓. Then write manifest. Total ≈ 1-3s. Blocking OK.

Also keep the call site BLOCKING: replace the spawn with direct await. Position: after ensure_installed (it needs mods list complete) and before launch. The launch flow already downloads version stuff after; add ~1-3s. Acceptable.

Let me update the code accordingly.

