HUGE FINDING:

1. **manifest VAR (46 satır)** ✓ — the launcher side WORKS! Modrinth icon URLs resolved and written.
2. **icons klasörü: 50 PNG** ✓ — downloads worked!

**BUT LOOK AT THE URLs:**
```
https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/x1hIzbuY/930154d1..._96.webp     ← WEBP!!
https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/8qkXwOnk/icon.png                  ← PNG ✓
https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/yBW8D80W/d4f5c3..._96.webp         ← WEBP!!
```

**MANY MODRINTH ICONS ARE .webp FILES!** And `NativeImage.read()` (class_1011.method_4309) — Minecraft's NativeImage **CANNOT decode WebP**! (MC supports PNG (and JPEG for some things? no — NativeImage is PNG-only via STBImage — stb_image supports PNG/JPG/BMP/PSD/TGA/GIF/HDR/PIC... does stb support webp? NO — stb_image does NOT support WebP!)

So: ~half the icons are .webp → NativeImage.read throws → register fails → FAILED → **letter badges**! That's exactly "hala ne logoları var" — rows show a mix: some real icons (PNG ones), mostly letter badges... wait — but 50 PNGs were downloaded by the LAUNCHER (the launcher downloads whatever bytes the URL returns — stores as .png name but content may be WEBP!). My naming saves every download as ".png" extension regardless of actual format!!! So MANY of those 50 "png" files are actually WEBP content → mod's NativeImage.read fails on them → badges.

ALSO — maybe worse: stb_image with WEBP bytes → returns null/throws → my register catch → FAILED ✓ badge (safe, no garbage).

**THE FIX — convert WebP → PNG on the LAUNCHER side (Rust):** The launcher already has the `image` crate in Cargo.toml: `image = { version = "0.25", features = ["png", "jpeg", "webp", "ico"] }` — **WEBP DECODE SUPPORT IS ALREADY THERE!** So in write_mod_icons: decode the downloaded bytes with `image::load_from_memory` (supports webp+png), re-encode as PNG, THEN write. All icons become real PNGs → mod reads all ✓.

